@@ -33,6 +33,22 @@ portfire table show.pf --catalog house.csv --rig autumn.rig --out panel.csv
 portfire pack  show.pf --catalog house.csv --rig autumn.rig --audience 200
 ```
 
+A show is designed against the catalog and fired out of whatever the store
+holds, so any of those commands will take the magazine book as well. Given one,
+every cue draws a unit in firing order, a cue the store cannot supply is covered
+by the nearest shell that can, and the sheets say which lot went in which tube.
+
+```
+portfire check show.pf --catalog house.csv --rig autumn.rig --magazine book.csv
+portfire sheet show.pf --catalog house.csv --rig autumn.rig --magazine book.csv
+portfire check show.pf --catalog house.csv --rig autumn.rig --magazine book.csv \\
+  --pull vn2405,vn2413
+```
+
+`--pull` sets lots aside before the draw, which is what a recall or a case
+dropped in the van means. `inventory` still counts what the show was designed
+on, because a stand in covers tonight and does not fill the order.
+
 A worked example lives in `examples/autumn`.
 
